---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import release from '../lib/release.json';
import build from '../lib/build.json';
import {composition,mountedApps} from '../lib/composition';

const lockDate = new Date(composition.reviewed + 'T00:00:00Z').toLocaleDateString('en-AU',{day:'numeric',month:'long',year:'numeric'});
---
<Base title="Verified release evidence" description="Actual source identities, deployed outcomes and remaining App Composer acceptance gates. Preparation and production are distinct."><h1>Show the working result.</h1><p class="lede">{release.state}</p><p>This Composer build is source <code>{build.commit}</code>.</p>
<section class="section"><h2>Serving now</h2><p>Composition <code>{composition.id.slice(0,12)}</code>, activated {lockDate}. Each mounted route serves the revision below; the same revision is returned by that route’s <code>build.json</code>.</p>
<div class="table-wrap"><table><thead><tr><th>Mounted route</th><th>App</th><th>Source revision</th></tr></thead><tbody>{mountedApps.map(app=><tr><td><a href={app.url}>{app.url.replace('https://','')}</a></td><td>{app.name} <span class="small">v{app.version}</span><br/><a href={app.repository}>Repository</a></td><td><code>{app.short}</code></td></tr>)}</tbody></table></div>
<p class="small">Editing this list by hand cannot change what runs. Update the pins by promoting a reviewed composition, which rewrites <code>composition.lock.json</code>.</p></section>
<section class="section"><h2>Verified outcomes</h2><p class="small">Recorded as observed. Entries keep the date they were reviewed and are not restamped when a later release ships.</p><ul>{release.verified.map(v=><li>{v}</li>)}</ul><p class="small">Historical verification reviewed {release.reviewed}.</p></section>
<section class="section"><h2>Open gates</h2><ul>{release.remaining.map(v=><li>{v}</li>)}</ul><p>The canonical issue evidence is maintained in <a href="https://github.com/loftwah/app-composer/issues/11">GitHub #11</a>. Current Worker identity is returned at <a href="/build.json">build.json</a>. Tests do not prove a physical device, commercial demand or a public multi-tenant security certification.</p></section></Base>
